{"id": "EUVD-2026-55674", "enisaUuid": "867d479e-2ce3-3603-84e9-aa1ae9b03ef3", "description": "A flaw was found in multicluster-global-hub. The manager component improperly validates the source identity of incoming CloudEvents on Kafka status topics. A remote attacker, after compromising a managed hub and obtaining its Kafka client certificate, can manipulate the self-asserted source identity. This allows the attacker to falsify or delete critical data, such as compliance, inventory, and cluster health information, belonging to other hubs in the database.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T16:41:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-29T16:43:50", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:L", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67516", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:67842", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:68515", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71597", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:73038", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:73419", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-71576", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2512513"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-71576", "GHSA-q5c4-r3vh-f379"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0149d2c8-47e3-3a36-b120-f51cbf228090", "product": {"name": "Multicluster Global Hub 1.7.3", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1788377424"}, {"id": "35e134cf-524c-322b-8640-12f7435579cf", "product": {"name": "Multicluster Global Hub 1.5.8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1789515288"}, {"id": "37bf5bac-737b-347b-b304-a3161a2f52b1", "product": {"name": "Multicluster Global Hub 1.6.6", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790086176"}, {"id": "625e2460-6c82-32e1-95fb-6ef5a1f66c84", "product": {"name": "Multicluster Global Hub 1.8.2", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1788359454"}, {"id":